Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||09-21-2001||12:28 PM||||My starter bascially fell apart and I bought a new one and had a local shop install it.  I hear a low rumble/puffing when starting it up.  The shop guy says he hears nothing unusual.  I told him it sounds nothing like it did before and asked him to realign the starter.  He kept it overnight and I came the next day to pick it up.  I started it up and it still sounded like crap.  He came out to try to hear what I am complaining about and still claims it sounds like any other car upon start up and that the starter can not be aligned anymore -- what his exact words were is "If we shimmy it anymore the teeth won't even hit the flywheel".  I said, well maybe it's already shimmied too much and needs to be closer.  He then told me that I don't know what I'm talking about and that ALL fiero's sound bad anyway.  What a Jerk.  Am I right on this?  Does the Starter need to be realigned, maybe REMOVE a shimmy that he stuck in there.  I can't believe how horrible it sounds on start up and that he denies hearing it.  Again, what a jerk!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Voytek||09-21-2001||02:11 PM||||I've been told all Fieros run hot.  Yeah, right!<P>What does the starter sound like?  I've never had a noisy one (had 5 Fieros).  I've had 2 die on my, but never sound bad.  Maybe it's not the shims, maybe it's the starter itself?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
