Z||000006||Master_Sushi||09-21-2001||11:05 PM||||Were all starters the same? Becuase the starters on my 88 coupe and 84 coupe sound completely diff. On my 84 when cranking it sounds REALLY low almost like a big rig starting. And on my 88 coupe it really somewhat high pitched and quiet. I really haven't thought anything of it, bucause I dont have any probs with either. I guess im just assuming they might not all sound the same?<P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000007||FieroFanaticus2||09-22-2001||01:18 AM||||A big rig discribes it perfectly.  But it used to sound just like a normal car starting up.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||09-22-2001||02:30 PM||||Some starters just make diferent sound than others.<P>You nearly always have fart around with GM starters a few times to get them shimmed right. You'll have to try diferent setups and see.<P>I'd definatly check it out. If the teeth aren't meshing deep enough you can break them off the ring gear. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||09-22-2001||09:02 PM||||It sounds like the "big rig" sounds come from either the wrong part, or a poor non-GM copy.<P>I went through two NAPA starters before I just bought one from GM.<P>That shop guy sounds like a jerk.  I would refuse to pay him, file a report with the BAR in your state, and take the car to a dealer who will not try to cheat and defraud you.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroFanaticus2||09-22-2001||09:31 PM||||I got mine from AutoZone,<BR>It's a reman.  DURALAST part #DL6312MS<BR>Only paid $40 for it plus a $30 core.<BR>But it was the best AutoZone had.  I've noticed AutoZone parts either don't fit correctly or are different sizes and shapes than the original as well, but the starter looked pretty much the same.<BR>What is the original Starter part # for an '88 coupe 4Cyl?  Or Atleast one that is a good replacement?  I think I am just going to get one from GM, return the one I have now, and have a pontiac dealer put on the new one.  Anyone know of a Discount GM Parts Dealer that I can get one from?<P><BR>||||reg||1
